        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Unlock Skettis and repeat Sha'tari Skyguard reputation farming to Exalted.\n\n1. Check Sha'tari Skyguard reputation. If already Exalted, skip to step 10. Otherwise speak to Yuula beside Shattrath's flight master (64.0, 42.0). Complete Threat from Above by killing the Gordunni ogres in the Barrier Hills north of the city, around 22.0, 12.0 on the Terokkar Forest map. Return and follow To Skettis to Blackwind Landing (64.0, 66.8).\n\n2. At Blackwind Landing, take World of Shadows from Severin. Kill Skettis arakkoa for 6 Shadow Dust and hand it in for Elixir of Shadows. Drink the elixir to see time-lost arakkoa, then keep it active while farming them.\n\n3. Kill Talonpriest Ishaal around 69.3, 78.5, loot Ishaal's Almanac and start its quest. Take it to Sky Commander Adaris at Blackwind Landing. Follow An Ally in Lower City to Rilak the Redeemed in Shattrath (52.6, 20.8), then return to Adaris with Countdown to Doom.\n\n4. Speak to Hazzik beside Adaris (64.2, 66.8). For Hazzik's Bargain, retrieve Hazzik's Package from the ground-level hut in UPPER Veil Shil'ak (74.8, 80.2), then return. The lower settlement and treetop platforms are the wrong search area.\n\n5. Take A Shabby Disguise. Use the supplied disguise, enter Sahaak's hut on the central island (67.0, 79.0), and buy Adversarial Bloodlines for 3 gold. Return the book to Hazzik and accept Adversarial Blood.\n\n6. With Elixir of Shadows active, kill time-lost arakkoa for 40 Time-Lost Scrolls per full summon cycle. At a SMALL Skull Pile, such as 69.6, 74.6, spend 10 scrolls to summon each of four different descendants: Darkscreecher Akkarai, Karrog, Gezzarak the Huntress and Vakkiz the Windrager. Loot their four different tokens.\n\n7. Give one of each token to Hazzik for a Time-Lost Offering. Complete Adversarial Blood first, then use Tokens of the Descendants for later exchanges. Take Terokk's Downfall from Adaris and use the LARGE Skull Pile on Terokk's Rest island (66.2, 77.5) with an Offering to summon Terokk.\n\n8. Defeat Terokk and turn in the quest. If he becomes immune, wait for the Skyguard bombing run and draw him into the blue fire to remove the shield. His large pile has a respawn delay of roughly 15 minutes; farm elsewhere between summons.\n\n9. Repeat arakkoa/treant kills, Shadow Dust hand-ins, the four-descendant exchanges and Terokk summons until Sha'tari Skyguard Exalted. Refresh the elixir. Bombing and escort dailies provide optional additional reputation; the repeatable route does not require waiting for daily resets. Scrolls and Offerings can also be bought from players.\n\n10. Buy Skyguard Tabard from Grella at Blackwind Landing (64.2, 66.2) for up to 1 gold before discounts and equip it. The same reputation unlocks the nether ray mounts, which are separate purchases.",
